-- title:
--   Regularity modulo (U) of elements outside (varpi,U)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number. Work in the ring `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ m)`, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ (formally `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\varpi^m)$, and let $s$ and $f$ be elements of it. Here `const (ϖ ^ m) ϖ` denotes the class of the constant power series $\varpi$, and `U (ϖ ^ m)` is the distinguished element of the model whose quotient is identified below with a one-variable power series ring. Assume that $s$ does not lie in the ideal generated by the two elements `const (ϖ ^ m) ϖ` and `U (ϖ ^ m)`, and that the product $s f$ lies in the principal ideal generated by `U (ϖ ^ m)`. The conclusion is that $f$ itself lies in the ideal generated by `U (ϖ ^ m)`.
--
--   This is the statement that, in the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ attached to a node of a semistable curve, any element outside $(\varpi,U)$ acts as a non-zero-divisor modulo the branch ideal $(U)$; equivalently $(U)$ behaves as a $(\varpi,U)$-primary ideal for multiplication by such elements. It is used in the analysis of the crossing model that produces, for elements outside $(\varpi,U)$, a unit times a power of $V$, and in the identification of the maximal ideal and of products as powers in the adically completed setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_mem_span_U_of_mul_mem_of_notMem.lean

